# Slice 346 (the book, forms-declare-or-call; the author 2026-11-10: "i: 6 это ошибка так как такого объявления быть
# не может"): i is a known place of an int, no Structure -- the form `i: 6` declares nothing and assigns nothing. Both
# executors refuse it where the traversal reaches it (the interpreter answers 8); the value is written by `i := 6`. The
# statement after the form does not use i: a run that accepted the form would end with success.
int: i 1
i: 6
int: after 1
